# Line endings
#
# Without this file the repository has no opinion on line endings, so whatever
# each machine happened to write got committed verbatim. The result was seven
# files (auth.py, camera.py, db.py, tcp_trigger_server.py, result_writer.py,
# logger.py, manage_users.py) stored with LF but sitting on disk as CRLF, which
# git reports as every single line changed - camera.py alone showed 1228
# modified lines while its content was byte-identical. Files that are
# permanently "modified" make the diff useless exactly when you need it, and
# hide the real change among thousands of phantom ones.
#
# text=auto means: decide per file whether it is text, normalise text to LF in
# the repository, and check it out in whatever form the platform wants. The
# working tree is unaffected on Windows once core.autocrlf=true is set; what
# changes is that git stops seeing a difference where there is none.
* text=auto

# Binary files. Marked explicitly rather than left to auto-detection: a false
# positive here does not produce a noisy diff, it corrupts the file by
# rewriting bytes that happen to look like line endings.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.bmp binary
*.tif binary
*.tiff binary
*.db binary
*.pt binary
*.pth binary
*.zip binary
